WEBVTT

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.190
There, there... It'll be okay, kiddo.

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:12.700
What a crybaby...

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:17.320
Takuya, you need to grow up
to be a big, strong boy!

00:00:19.490 --> 00:00:22.620
Don't scare him like that.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.500
You're such a good boy, Takuya...

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.340
My beautiful little baby...

00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:18.490
"Episode 1"

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:18.030
Some famous doctor once said that dreams

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:20.760
are manifestations of repressed desires.

00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:22.550
If that's true,

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.510
then what does a dream 
of my dead parents mean?

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:32.920
Blue skies and white... panties?

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.250
You're skipping class again?

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:37.910
Would you stand up?

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:42.430
Maybe, if you help me get these pants off.

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:44.880
That would make something
else stand up, wouldn't it?

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:46.680
You get it.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:49.640
You're a terrible student.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:51.190
You say that,

00:02:51.190 --> 00:02:55.320
but a grown-up like you
doesn't freak out over it, huh?

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:03.470
I heard about your dad.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:04.670
I'm sorry.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:08.240
I wish there was something I could say...

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:11.540
Well, it's easier than just
having him stay missing forever.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:14.590
At least I have an answer.

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:16.590
I see.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.260
Dying in a cave-in during his research
was more or less

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:21.650
how I expected him to go.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.890
Is that all you came to say?

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:28.930
No, I've got a problem I want your help with.

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.310
And I've got a different kind of problem...

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.020
No.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:35.440
Teenage boys' problems can be very serious.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.570
A transfer student is coming.

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:40.650
Now? Right before summer break?

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.400
Well, she has her reasons.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.370
And I want you to look after her.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.370
No. Why should I?

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:50.370
That's a shame! She's really cute, too...

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.280
Then I'll do it gladly!

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.100
I thought you'd say that.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:04:01.120
Arima-<i>sama</i>, please come to
the Historical Research Department.

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:07.720
Boss!

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.230
Why did you quit the kendo team?

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:12.890
Leave me alone, Yuki.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:14.980
I've got bigger problems now.

00:04:14.980 --> 00:04:18.230
That's right. You just got
called on the intercom.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:21.280
Could it be over that one thing?
Or maybe that other thing...

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:25.410
I was so sure they'd
never find that out, though!

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:28.240
It's worrying how many 
possibilities there are.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:32.830
Come on, join the kendo team again!

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:36.840
I only did kendo because my dad told me to.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:40.340
And now he's gone.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.340
So I'm done with it.

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:50.350
But you're in more than
one club too, aren't you?

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:54.020
That's right. I'm in the
historical research club.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.230
You're after Mio, aren't you?

00:04:57.690 --> 00:05:00.400
I know you've got a crush on her.

00:05:00.730 --> 00:05:02.030
Go make her yours.

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:04.170
Make her mine...?

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.450
Lately there's been that
curse thing and the lightning strikes.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:10.870
She and I have been going
around looking into it.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:12.370
I'm having a great time, honestly!

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:15.370
She loves that paranormal stuff.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:16.620
That's right!

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:20.330
Wait, boss. You sure know
a lot about Shimazu-<i>san</i>.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:21.920
Don't tell me...

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:24.210
No way in hell do I want 
to date that ice queen.

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:25.840
Yeah, that's right!

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:29.640
But you know,
Shimazu-<i>san</i>'s nice to everybody else,

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.140
but she's really mean to you.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:34.640
Shimazu-<i>san</i>!

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:35.490
Hey.

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:38.730
Milady.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:41.070
Stop calling me that, please.

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:43.400
Then how about "Mio-<i>chan</i>, the school idol!"

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.910
Why do you make me so mad?

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:50.280
Not sure.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:51.910
That time of the month?

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:54.330
How crude!

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:58.830
--What time of the month 
did you think I meant?

00:05:54.830 --> 00:05:58.830
--Listening to the two of them
talk takes years off your life.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.630
Yuki-<i>kun</i>, let's go!

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:01.630
O-Of course!

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:04.010
Have a nice day, boss!

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:10.260
What? They called me to an empty room?

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:20.650
You may enter.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:21.690
It's me, Arima.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:22.560
Excuse me.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:23.270
What?

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:25.230
Ayumi-<i>san</i>...

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.780
Oh? Takuya-<i>kun</i>, what are you doing here?

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:29.860
Well, um...

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:31.450
They called me on the intercom.

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:34.030
What? Did you do something again?

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:37.000
No, I haven't done anything lately.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:42.040
Aww... You know, it makes it hard for me
as your mother when you act that way.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:46.960
They were calling for me, not you.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.530
About Geotechnics' construction project.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:52.780
I heard it was having a lot of issues.

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:56.810
Yeah. Weird things keep happening.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:00.480
I need to go do an inspection 
right after this.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.230
You're heading to the coast, too?

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:03.060
Yeah.

00:07:03.060 --> 00:07:06.440
I don't want to be the kind of boss
who just sits where it's safe

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:07.860
and tells other people what to do.

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:21.540
It's good to see you again, Ryuzoji-<i>sensei</i>.

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:24.540
It's been a long time, Ayumi-<i>kun</i>.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:27.050
I'm glad I caught the two of you together.

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:31.630
I want to talk about Kodai...
No, about Dr. Arima.

00:07:32.010 --> 00:07:33.120
About my dad?

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:38.660
I worked alongside
Dr. Arima in his research for years.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:45.110
If you'll allow it,
I'd like to carry on his work.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:48.110
I'm sure he'd be happy to hear that.

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:50.990
It's the best thing I can do to remember him.

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:56.320
I'd like you send his
research notes to my house.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:59.300
Of course, I'll pay the costs.

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:01.500
I'll have arrangements made immediately.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:04.330
I do have a question.

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:08.250
Is there anything Dr. Arima
gave you to keep, specifically?

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:11.290
No, I can't think of anything.

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:14.010
Me either.

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:15.500
What sort of thing are you thinking of?

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:20.150
Some sort of archaeological relic.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:22.700
Relic?

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:27.330
Takuya.

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:29.120
Mitsuki-<i>san</i>!

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.010
It's been so long!

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:34.110
Should I call you "Arima-<i>kun</i>" now?

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:35.910
Just call me Takuya.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.490
It really has been forever.

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:41.540
I quit my job as a part-time lecturer here.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.780
Don't tell me it's because of that?

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.000
No!

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:49.460
I'm just a lot busier in my job
as Ryuzoji-<i>sensei</i>'s secretary.

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:50.420
I see.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.510
I heard about your father.

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:56.220
I thought you'd be more depressed.

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:57.640
And if I was?

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:02.390
I'd make you feel better again.

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:05.690
Hang in there.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:07.350
You too.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:11.110
It's clear what the decision is for me.

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:12.220
Bye.

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:20.950
Hi there.

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:24.170
What are you thoughts on
Geotech's construction project?

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.260
Oh...

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:30.130
It sucks I can't go to the
beach over summer vacation!

00:09:30.130 --> 00:09:31.750
Give back our summer!

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:34.010
Give back our girls in swimsuits!

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:35.470
Thanks.

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:36.820
That was perfect.

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:41.660
I'm home.

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:47.300
What's this?

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:50.730
This size... This weight...

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:51.730
It's gotta be!

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:52.860
An adult...

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:57.610
Ahem, an <i>artistic</i> video of girls posing!

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:59.580
Well done, Yuki!

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:02.990
What is this?

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:12.290
Hello?

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:19.050
Hello?

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:21.660
What was that about?

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:26.810
Shimazu-<i>san</i>, let's go home.

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:29.260
Just a little longer.

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:40.720
This flower again...

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:46.320
And now, a special report on Sakaimachi.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.960
We go live to Kaori Asakura at the scene!

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:50.790
"More Accidents.
More questions about management."

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:51.380
--I'm here at the coastal construction site.
--Halt the construction!

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:52.250
--Halt the construction!

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:54.290
--That's the girl I just saw.
--Halt the construction!

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.880
--The demonstrations calling
for an end to the construction
--Listen to local voices!

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:59.930
--are likely to only get more fierce from here.
--Listen to local voices!

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:03.510
It sucks I can't go to the
beach over summer vacation!

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:05.100
Give back our summer!

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:07.620
--Give back our girls in swimsuits!
--Seriously?

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:11.900
Look! That's Ayumi Arima,
the manager of the construction project.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:21.110
"Geotechnics Coastal Construction Project"

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:17.030
--Geotechnics is working to
identify the cause of the accidents...

00:11:15.590 --> 00:11:17.030
--Huh? The clouds...

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:17.860
What is that?

00:11:17.860 --> 00:11:19.320
Look! It's glowing!

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:25.870
--This is unbelievable!
Lightning has just struck the area!
--Somebody get an ambulance!

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:28.500
--This is unbelievable!
Lightning has just struck the area!
--We told you this would happen!

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:29.370
Run!

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:34.790
Ayumi-<i>san</i>!

00:11:43.590 --> 00:11:46.060
It's dangerous here!
Please don't get any closer!

00:11:47.430 --> 00:11:48.970
You there! No pushing!

00:11:55.690 --> 00:11:57.780
Hey, you, stay out of there!

00:11:57.780 --> 00:11:58.910
I'm family!

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:01.240
Okay, take care.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:02.110
Thank you.

00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:05.510
Takuya-<i>kun</i>!

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:07.830
I saw what happened on TV...

00:12:07.830 --> 00:12:09.080
Are you okay?

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:12.620
--Yes, I'm just fin--
--You! Kid!

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:14.330
You're not allowed in here!

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:15.790
Toyotomi-<i>kun</i>.

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:18.880
I'm sorry. This is my son.

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:22.130
Oh, he's your son?

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:24.180
It looks like you've raised him well.

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:28.850
But I'm site foreman, and you can't
come in here without my permission--

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:30.040
I'm leaving in a second.

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:32.480
I appreciate it.

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.820
So he's "Useless Flunky A"
in the end credits, huh?

00:12:37.820 --> 00:12:40.190
Don't say that!

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:43.740
Takuya-<i>kun</i>, I'm not going
to be back until late again tonight.

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:45.820
Okay. Don't push yourself too hard.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:48.620
Eat dinner without me.

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:53.020
Boss!

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:55.340
Oh, you came to see?

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:58.960
Did you see that lightning blast?

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:00.840
Yeah. On TV.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.060
That's why I came here.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:05.160
Did you see anything strange?

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:06.510
Not really.

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:09.810
We were over at the shrine...

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:13.390
That lightning didn't seem natural, did it?

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:14.700
Not natural?

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:20.480
That place is dangerous.

00:13:26.360 --> 00:13:28.250
You should stay away from it.

00:13:37.370 --> 00:13:38.630
You know her?

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:39.380
Nope.

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:59.520
An archaeological something-or-other, huh?

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:02.940
What do you think the 
transfer student's like?

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:05.690
You were just wishing
it was a hot guy, weren't you?

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:07.410
I was not!

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:11.100
Okay, everybody. Sit down.

00:14:13.470 --> 00:14:16.500
Welcome, transfer student!

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:26.260
Arima, she's sitting next to you.

00:14:26.540 --> 00:14:28.010
Takuya gave it his all...

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:29.260
And still got no reaction?

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:30.760
That girl's kind of impressive.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:37.810
"Kanna"

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:35.060
Kanna Hatano.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.310
Nice to meet you all.

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:40.940
Girls, no getting jealous because she's cute.

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:43.230
Guys, wait a while before
you make a move on her. Got it?

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:45.860
Okay, time to start homeroom...

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:50.200
--So, who's on helper duty today...

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:50.200
--We met yesterday, didn't we?

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:53.200
Sensei, Kanna-<i>san</i>'s not here today.

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:57.870
--Tell your mother that she should
call off the construction project.

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:56.800
--Okay, Kazuki.

00:14:57.280 --> 00:14:57.960
--Okay!

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:01.130
--Come to the teacher's office to get
everybody's summer homework later.

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:01.320
--There'll be

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:03.460
another accident.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:07.970
I'm glad to see you're so happy!

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:14.600
Do you think Arima-<i>kun</i> would
join the historical research club?

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:15.890
You want my boss to join?

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:21.400
His father, Kodai Arima, 
was a famous historian.

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:24.480
I'd love to see his research notes...

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:27.110
Oh, that's why.

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:27.820
What?

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:29.310
No, nothing.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:31.680
Excuse me.

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:33.620
Arima-<i>kun</i>!

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:34.660
Boss!

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:35.990
Don't tell me you're joining the club?

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:37.240
Yes!

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:38.720
Not a chance.

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:41.000
Where's Ryuzoji-<i>san</i>?

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:43.880
I heard he's not here right now.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:44.770
I see.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:46.920
Is something going on?

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.590
No. I'll come back later.

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:50.370
Bye!

00:15:51.050 --> 00:15:52.350
Boss!

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:08.580
I'm home.

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:13.910
Again?

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:18.320
Sheesh... now what is it?

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:24.830
"Parallel World Constitutive Theorem"?

00:16:23.170 --> 00:16:26.840
"Parallel World Constitutive Theorem -
Reflector Device Construction"

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:27.430
"Reflector Device Construction"?

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:28.170
"ACU Professor Yurika Imagawa"

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:36.680
"Time is reversible. History is not."

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:40.850
What am I reading?

00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:43.680
They didn't write this 
to be understood at all.

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:51.660
Reflector... Device?

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:55.740
"To my beloved idiot of a son."

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:55.310
Dad?

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:04.250
By the time you read this,
I'll have disappeared.

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:08.250
But that doesn't mean I'm dead.

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:10.980
My dad is alive?

00:17:12.560 --> 00:17:17.720
Gather the jewels, and go to
the base of Ken-no-misaki tonight.

00:17:17.720 --> 00:17:20.500
You should find someone 
waiting for you there.

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:23.140
Tonight at 10?

00:17:30.230 --> 00:17:35.650
"Stop the Construction"

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:51.280
Hello! Dad!

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:53.710
Sheesh.

00:18:03.810 --> 00:18:05.810
Is that my dad in disguise?

00:18:06.230 --> 00:18:07.890
Probably not.

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:10.220
Hey, are you okay?

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:14.710
Were you going for a night swim?

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:19.270
Her ears...

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:22.530
Are you okay?

00:18:27.410 --> 00:18:28.180
Um...

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:33.100
Y-Yuno...

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:35.020
"You know"?

00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:37.020
What are you saying?

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:46.060
W-Wait!

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:47.910
You can't just...

00:18:58.900 --> 00:18:59.820
This...

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:01.790
This is impossible!

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:04.030
I see.

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:08.320
So she was abandoned
at the far end of causality?

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:11.360
What are you doing here, Takuya-<i>kun</i>?

00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:13.680
Who was that girl?

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:16.210
That's what I want to know.

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:19.840
Everything is as Kodai Arima planned it.

00:19:19.840 --> 00:19:22.670
Just like that thing you're holding.

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:26.060
What is "that thing"?

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:31.420
Kodai should have left you something
that allows you to cross Neumann space.

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:33.730
What are you talking about?

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:37.940
Kodai realized the existence
of a law that controls this world.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:41.240
The mother that gave birth
to you gave him the inspiration.

00:19:41.240 --> 00:19:42.740
Takuya-<i>kun</i>'s...

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:43.740
Mother?

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:50.130
Your mother and Kodai still live
in a world different from our own.

00:19:52.420 --> 00:19:54.250
How do you know?

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:57.670
The thing you hold is the answer.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:01.970
And I

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:05.040
must have it.

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:07.500
Ryuzoji-<i>sensei</i>!

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.050
Seriously?

00:20:09.730 --> 00:20:12.250
That's not a cigarette lighter, is it?

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:16.480
Tell me one thing, at least.

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:17.370
Very well.

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:21.670
Can you use this to find my dad?

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:23.380
Correct.

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:31.330
It's the only device that can see
the infinite possibilities of spacetime.

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:38.550
We're done talking.

00:20:40.710 --> 00:20:41.580
An earthquake?

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:45.050
Is this... resonance?

00:20:51.640 --> 00:20:54.020
Did that girl who just
disappeared do something?

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:05.410
Give me the device! Now!

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:08.910
Kanna-<i>chan</i>?

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:31.500
Ryuzoji? Ayumi-<i>san</i>!

00:21:32.730 --> 00:21:33.310
Huh?

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:37.120
My head!

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:43.580
This is a seriously nasty headache...

00:21:57.210 --> 00:21:58.260
Ayumi-<i>san</i>?

00:21:58.710 --> 00:22:01.880
Hello, this is your wake-up call!

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:03.300
What do you want?

00:22:03.590 --> 00:22:07.930
Huh? You're in a bad mood this morning, boss.

00:22:07.930 --> 00:22:10.600
It's summer break tomorrow!

00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:12.560
I've got bigger problems!

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:14.350
I'm on my way to the cops.

00:22:14.350 --> 00:22:17.940
What, did they get you for underage smoking?

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:21.110
It's not about me. It's Ayumi-<i>san</i>.

00:22:21.110 --> 00:22:22.610
My mother is...

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:23.980
Oh yeah.

00:22:24.230 --> 00:22:28.070
I love to watch her walk.

00:22:28.070 --> 00:22:31.450
She always moves so briskly,
like a brisk autumn breeze!

00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:34.410
What did you say?

00:22:34.410 --> 00:22:36.120
Like a brisk autumn breeze!

00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:37.370
Not that!

00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:39.040
What did you say about Ayumi-<i>san</i>?

00:22:39.040 --> 00:22:43.540
Your mom just walked 
right past me, briskly...

00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:48.050
So it seems.

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:50.260
Oh, Sensei, you're so silly!

00:22:50.260 --> 00:22:51.260
Ayumi-<i>san</i>!

00:22:51.260 --> 00:22:52.970
Oh, Takuya-<i>kun</i>!

00:22:55.930 --> 00:22:58.190
You look pale.

00:22:58.190 --> 00:23:01.770
Why are you staring at his face?

00:23:02.140 --> 00:23:05.860
Because of what happened 
last night, obviously!

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:07.530
Last night?

00:23:08.610 --> 00:23:13.580
Oh, Ayumi-<i>kun</i> completely 
blew off our meeting.

00:23:13.580 --> 00:23:15.370
She seems busy.

00:23:15.370 --> 00:23:17.120
I'm so sorry.

00:23:17.330 --> 00:23:19.880
What are you talking about?

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:23.540
Takuya-<i>kun</i>, hang in there.

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:25.670
That's what Kodai wants, I'm sure.

00:23:26.410 --> 00:23:27.920
What's going on?

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:31.800
Do they not remember
what happened yesterday?

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:41.570
"Episode 2:
Parallel World Constitutive Theorem."

00:23:35.810 --> 00:23:39.130
Episode 2:
"Parallel World Constitutive Theorem."
